WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.867
Run this query and compare the original admit timestamp with the formatted strings.

00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:08.047
The first label is designed for human readability.

00:00:08.047 --> 00:00:11.187
The second creates ISO-style date text.

00:00:11.187 --> 00:00:17.017
Both outputs are text. The original admit time remains the typed analytical value.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.567
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.762
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:22.762 --> 00:00:27.407
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:27.407 --> 00:00:33.962
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:33.962 --> 00:00:35.752
daylight-saving changes.
